From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: theycallmeboxy <82409831+theycallmeboxy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 04:56:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] pan/afbc: compress single-channel 32-bit colour formats on
 v9+

AFBC is type agnostic on v9+: pan_afbc_format() converts every format to
its UNORM twin before choosing a mode. R32_FLOAT, R32_UINT and R32_SINT
become R32_UNORM, which had no mode, so these images were never
compressed. Shadow maps and other single-channel float targets are
common: Warhammer 40,000: Gladius renders two 2048x2048 R32_FLOAT shadow
maps per frame and blurs them, all uncompressed.

Compress R32_UNORM in the R8G8B8A8 mode, as Z32_FLOAT already is: AFBC
keeps the raw bits, the decompression mode follows the image's mode so
any 32-bit view reads back the same bits, and YTR only applies to RGB
formats.

Purpose: performance: single-channel 32-bit colour images (R32_FLOAT/UINT/SINT; shadow maps) are AFBC-compressed in the R8G8B8A8 mode on v9+, like Z32_FLOAT, instead of stored uncompressed
Upstream-commit: none
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (Anbernic RG477M, Dimensity 8300, v11)
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21 / MediaTek
Dependencies: applies after rg477m/050 (shared Panfrost AFBC table, src/panfrost/lib/pan_afbc.h; the GL driver is not used on this device)
Validation test: test build afbc32 (same code): PanProbe 38/38 x2; vkd3d-proton 2.14.1 suite identical per test to 001-049 (309 PASS); Warhammer 40,000: Gladius (native Vulkan, two 2048x2048 R32_FLOAT shadow maps per frame) turn 1 interleaved 42.7/43.3/44.0 vs 41.2/40.4/42.2/40.2 fps (+5.6%, no overlap), shadows render, traced shadow blur 872 -> 762 us; gameplay sweep in range: Portal 2 182.9/169.6, Megabonk 80.3, Moonlighter 135.7, ROLLERDROME 90.0 (no R32 targets in that game; 049 code 88.9 the same hour), Fallout NV 27.5, Tomb Raider benchmark 74.6, no GPU faults
Channel: compatibility, unsafe
Generated-by: LLM
---
 src/panfrost/lib/pan_afbc.h | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/lib/pan_afbc.h b/src/panfrost/lib/pan_afbc.h
index 524ca19b..6c5bed86 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/lib/pan_afbc.h
+++ b/src/panfrost/lib/pan_afbc.h
@@ -596,6 +596,10 @@ pan_afbc_format(unsigned arch, enum pipe_format format, unsigned plane_idx)
    case PIPE_FORMAT_Z16_UNORM:         return PAN_AFBC_MODE_R8G8;
 
    case PIPE_FORMAT_Z32_FLOAT:         return PAN_AFBC_MODE_R8G8B8A8;
+   /* Single-channel 32-bit colour (R32_FLOAT/UINT/SINT, all R32_UNORM here
+    * on v9+) is compressed as raw 32-bit pixels, like Z32_FLOAT. */
+   case PIPE_FORMAT_R32_UNORM:
+      return arch >= 9 ? PAN_AFBC_MODE_R8G8B8A8 : PAN_AFBC_MODE_INVALID;
    case PIPE_FORMAT_Z24_UNORM_S8_UINT: return PAN_AFBC_MODE_R8G8B8A8;
    case PIPE_FORMAT_Z24X8_UNORM:       return PAN_AFBC_MODE_R8G8B8A8;
    case PIPE_FORMAT_X24S8_UINT:        return PAN_AFBC_MODE_R8G8B8A8;
